SUMMARY:Layer The Walls: Turn of the Century
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, November 21\, 2026 • 3 PM • Steinman Hall In one
  Lower East Side tenement\, forty layers of wallpaper were found clinging 
 to the walls\, each piece applied by a new immigrant family. Using puppetr
 y\, masks\, and live action\, Layer the Walls tells the incredible stories
  held within each layer—an Irish immigrant helping to build the Brooklyn
  Bridge\, Italian brothers surviving the Great Blizzard of 1888\, and two 
 Russian Jewish garment workers joining the Uprising of 20\,000 to fight fo
 r safety. Recommended for ages 8 and up. 2 PM • Lobby • Free kids’ a
 ctivities and crafts! Tickets: Adults $15 • Students: $10 Accessibility:
  ASL interpretation\, sensory-friendly accommodations\, and audio descript
 ion will be available. There will be a pre-show touch tour for blind and l
 ow-vision patrons. Please get in touch with Barry Kornhauser to learn more
 .\n\nPrice: $10 to $15\n\nSchedule listed: Sat\, Nov 21\, 2026 03:00 PM ES
